Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:24:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-44: a resize handle with several selected resizes
 all of them (0.44.0)

WinForms / WPF: dragging a resize handle of the primary with a multi-
selection changes every selected component by the same amount -- as
Ctrl+arrows already did here. Before, only the primary changed. Now the
handle's drag carries the group (the form, which is never in a group,
resizes alone), a locked member stops the whole drag as a move does, and
the result is ONE batch edit = one undo step.

Also checked: the all-pages sweep in real VS Code after R28-R36 -- 83 pages,
189 pass / 0 fail, no page-JS errors, nothing saved, the sources' MD5
unchanged.

Test: probe (2 selected, the SE handle dragged +12 / +6 with Alt: both
widths +12, both heights +6, one batch of 2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
